:detective: Not blocking, and not something this PR introduced, but this function is now simple enough to make it cheap.

`toValidUTF8String` runs per row for every `Tuple` element name and every `Map` key, and twice each time: in `countBSONFieldSize` (lines 244 and 274) and again in `serializeField` (lines 482 and 512). Every call builds a `WriteBufferFromOwnString` and a `WriteBufferValidUTF8` and copies the name byte by byte. For a `Map` column that is several allocations per key per row, just to return the name unchanged in almost every case.

Most names are ASCII without a zero byte, and then the result equals the input. A fast path would skip the buffers:

```cpp
static String toValidUTF8String(const String & name)
{
    /// Nothing to replace or escape.
    if (isAllASCII(reinterpret_cast<const UInt8 *>(name.data()), name.size()) && name.find('\0') == String::npos)
        return name;
    ...
}
```

(`isAllASCII` is in `Common/StringUtils.h`; it accepts the zero byte, hence the second check.)

`Tuple` element names also do not depend on the row, so they could be converted once per type instead of per row. That takes more plumbing; the fast path above already removes most of the cost.

Fine as a follow-up if you'd rather keep this PR to the escaping fix.
